  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Integration decision making"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What is integration decision making?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The hardest part of integration is deciding which technique to use\n- There are lots of them!"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/08/8.2.11-Notes-meth_mess.png",
   "file": "assets/cda187b292b6-8-2-11-notes-meth-mess.png",
   "alt": "Notes meth_mess, downloadable AS & A Level Maths revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I know which integration method to use?"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/08/8.2.11-Notes-int_2main.png",
   "file": "assets/2b023a07ba3a-8-2-11-notes-int-2main.png",
   "alt": "Notes int_2main, downloadable AS & A Level Maths revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The main two requirements for success with integration are\n\n  - **Experience**\n  - **Familiarity**\n- Always check for Reverse Chain Rule …\n\n  - … particularly after changing part of an integral …\n  - … by using a trig identity for example"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/08/8.2.11-Notes-int_flow.png",
   "file": "assets/96f0492e2923-8-2-11-notes-int-flow.png",
   "alt": "Notes int_flow, downloadable AS & A Level Maths revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "Key to diagram above:"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "(1) Powers of $x$**   **"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "(2) Substitution"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "(3) Obvious substitution"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "(4) Trig"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "(5) Algebraic Division"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "(6) $\\frac{f'(x)}{f(x)}$"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "(7) Partial fractions"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "(8) Integration by Parts"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "(9) Reverse Chain Rule"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "- If in doubt, try something … You may gain marks for attempting a suitable substitution.\n- You may gain marks from using a trig identity.\n- You may gain marks from attempting to simplify or rewrite a fraction."
  },
